17592186045417] [17592186500258 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bb295803-371c-5d9e-af5b-4a4e5e12624f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500282 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500282 #edb/ref 1069 "q-349315" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500282 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500282 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e4/e4335622f7505350155fd5c84ce1cbdbb6c4fba4570b8cf4a4cd8982403ffede.png)\n\nAn aquarium has $45$ fish. The ratio of goldfish to guppies is shown in the diagram above. How many guppies are in the aquarium?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500282 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "05816576-2c37-58bb-af9f-d158df6b7282" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500282 #edb/ref 1074 "The tape diagram shows $2$ boxes corresponding to goldfish, and $3$ boxes corresponding to guppies. Therefore, the ratio of goldfish to guppies is $2:3.$\n\nWe are told that there are $45$ fish in total. The tape diagram has $2+3=5$ boxes in total. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $45÷5=9$ fish.\n\nNow, we fill the number $9$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/06/069481a1ab6b18ebe6bf20053b793c49b54c06352f3acfc218aae32e34cd8f50.png)\n\nSince there are $3$ boxes corresponding to guppies, and each box represents $9$ fish, the number of guppies must be:\n\n$$\n3\\times 9=27.\n$$\n\nSo, there are $27$ guppies in the aquarium." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500284 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500284 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61538" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500284 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500284 #edb/ref 1071 "Danny and Sheilah are making donuts. Danny makes $4$ donuts for every $5$ donuts Sheilah makes. Which tape diagram represents the given scenario?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500284 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0da3c985-9149-5021-920d-90e4d419fc72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500284 #edb/ref 1074 "We are told that:\n\nDanny makes $4$ donuts for every $5$ donuts Sheilah makes.\n\nSo, in a tape diagram, Danny's tape must contain $4$ boxes, while the tape corresponding to Sheilah should have $5$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the diagram is the following:\n\n![](images/29/290ed3e67984cefd45affab89efb929baff403ba762885551a1ca4eb3d61e7ab.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500285 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500285 #edb/ref 1069 "q-349283" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500285 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500285 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/55/556822d04577fef44f422814f5880fb885602bd6ea597f178b33df6bda4e11ba.png)\n\nThe tape diagram above shows the ratio between red and blue marbles in Noah's collection. What is the ratio of red marbles to blue marbles?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500285 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0eac2215-e323-598c-aeac-4408994fc7bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500285 #edb/ref 1074 "The tape diagram for red marbles shows $3$ boxes while the tape for blue marbles contains $6$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of red marbles to blue marbles is $3:6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500287 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500287 #edb/ref 1069 "q-92780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500287 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500287 #edb/ref 1071 "Mary and Tina are riding their bikes, both going at a steady pace. Every second,  Mary travels $4$ meters  while Tina  travels $3$ meters. Which tape diagram represents the given scenario?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500287 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "15b8eebd-946d-5aa5-9960-ed6597145975" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500287 #edb/ref 1074 "We are told that: \n\nEvery second,  Mary travels $4$ meters  while Tina  travels $3$ meters \n\nSo, in a tape diagram, Mary's tape must contain $4$ boxes, while the tape corresponding to Tina should have $3$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the diagram is the following:\n\n![](images/23/23498cdbf112703b7ca7cf6bce275a83b0ad8f7a63df73007dcd5f010bb3c69d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500291 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500291 #edb/ref 1069 "q-92809" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500291 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500291 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/9b/9b349ac221e04877ef3ad0474d9ddb1e95e7f01748f0be9975e18b9195090f5e.png)\n\nMs. Robinson's class has $32$ students. The ratio of boys to girls  is shown in the diagram above. How many girls are in Ms. Robinson's class?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500291 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1a689f52-7a55-519b-a705-abe55d84d915" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500291 #edb/ref 1074 "The tape diagram shows $3$ boxes corresponding to boys, and $5$ boxes corresponding to girls. Therefore, the ratio of boys to girls born is $3:5.$\n\nWe are told that Ms. Robinson's class has $32$ students in total. The tape diagram has $3+5=8$ boxes in total. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $32÷8=4$ students in Ms. Robinson's class. \n\nNow, we fill the number $4$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/66/66ba3f4ea51eb34cf4c1f313058e56523236ebd36fcd092082b9f6ca63261d1b.png)\n\nSince there are $5$ boxes corresponding to girls, and each box represents $4$ students, the number of girls in Mr. Robinson's class must be:\n\n$$\n5\\times 4=20.\n$$\n\nSo, there are $20$  girls in Mr. Robinson's class." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500294 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500294 #edb/ref 1069 "q-92726" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500294 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500294 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/14/146a01a45a5984dec5db93ede46ee67a84eb2a4ccc1d7e3abeafbcfd1f55a65b.png)\n\nThe tape diagram above shows the ratio between the number of Yes and No answers obtained in a survey of several kids about whether they liked the movie The Mega Titanium Man. What is the ratio of the number of Yes answers to  the total number of responses?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500294 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "22cfb00e-d576-505c-8cf4-a3b624bb7d83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500294 #edb/ref 1074 "The tape diagram for Yes answers shows $6$ boxes while the tape diagram has $6+4=10$ boxes in total.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of Yes to all answers is $6:10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500295 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500295 #edb/ref 1069 "q-92772" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500295 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500295 #edb/ref 1071 "A fan noticed the following trend: in the last three weeks, the Yankees won $4$ games for every $3$ Red Sox wins.  Which tape diagram represents the given scenario?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500295 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "24b62cd6-a2c3-5060-a0de-7e8afa941a63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500295 #edb/ref 1074 "We are told that:\n\nthe Yankees won $4$ games for every $3$  Red Sox wins  \n\nSo, in a tape diagram, Yankee's tape must contain $4$ boxes, while the tape corresponding to the Red Sox should have $3$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the diagram is the following:\n\n![](images/e5/e53d8287e51e697be1a010a7af34ad2a062bc505ce06326e15605ac52bd16cda.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500297 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500297 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61476" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500297 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500297 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e7/e79f93d06560ea1a95116c0278e5536c4b629aa3ee04a24abc3c4a9f0f97b693.png)\n\nBarbie made a cake that had candied fruit and raisins. The ratio of candied fruit to raisins is given by the tape diagram above.  If she used $8$ ounces of candied fruit to make the cake, how many ounces of raisins did she use?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500297 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "29d68311-d734-5664-956b-1dbe021c610a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500297 #edb/ref 1074 "We are told that Barbie used $8$ ounces of candied fruit in total. The tape diagram shows $4$ boxes for candied fruit. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $8÷4=2$ ounces.   \n\nNow, we fill the number $2$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/7c/7c40be92924cb2cebf8661802933280b59a843c3d0ab3616088c2a5643404449.png)\n\n \n\nSince there are $5$ boxes corresponding to raisins, and each box represents $2$ ounces, the number of ounces of raisins used was\n:\n\n$$\n5\\times 2=10\n$$\n\nSo, Barbie used $10$ ounces of raisins." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500313 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500313 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61532" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500313 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500313 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/38/3887946edaafb7d94bbf911c53cf1a0d2a48d43880829ce6069cc42d26eba526.png)\n\nTimmy set up a one-day lemonade sale in front of his house.  The ratio of disposable cups to lemonade servings is given by the tape diagram above. If he had a total of $40$ disposable cups to begin with, how many lemonade servings did he have then?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500313 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53afd0b5-618f-512e-b769-550096e6ab34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500313 #edb/ref 1074 "We are told that there were $40$ disposable cups in total. The tape diagram for those shows $5$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $40÷5=8$ disposable cups.   \n\nNow, we fill the number $8$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/b3/b3ed4d72509ba29446f6da8919d81b4cce2dc57d6b80c8496f832c2ec5e95616.png)\n\nSince there are $6$ boxes corresponding to lemonade servings, and each box represents $8$ servings, the number of servings was:\n\n$$\n6\\times 8=48\n$$\n\nSo, Timmy had $48$ lemonade servings in total." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500319 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500319 #edb/ref 1069 "q-349312" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500319 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500319 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ea/ea20fd21d0d8924163615500ebf0c5aaa1823a68121c0fc574624dfd8182fbf6.png)\n\nA box contains $25$ colored pencils. The ratio of red pencils to blue pencils is shown in the diagram above. How many blue pencils are in the box?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500319 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "73f7645f-5556-5602-99d1-a98b9d1aa7ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500319 #edb/ref 1074 "The tape diagram shows $3$ boxes corresponding to red pencils, and $2$ boxes corresponding to blue pencils. Therefore, the ratio of red to blue pencils is $3:2.$\n\nWe are told that there are $25$ pencils in total. The tape diagram has $3+2=5$ boxes in total. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $25÷5=5$ pencils.\n\nNow, we fill the number $5$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/58/58a4e9ce8130b4e84307652c4237e0d898cfb56a9f25ab00669d376b3bfb4515.png)\n\nSince there are $2$ boxes corresponding to blue pencils, and each box represents $5$ pencils, the number of blue pencils must be:\n\n$$\n2\\times 5=10\n$$\n\nSo, there are $10$ blue pencils in the box." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500354 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500354 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61523" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500354 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500354 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/03/03b73d8213a55e4a50885b80b8f031de3186e46d9b358be792c2043b1c8a97b8.png)\n\nThe tape diagram above shows the ratio between the number of liters of milk and juice that Bob buys in a month. If he buys $16$ liters of milk in a month, how many liters of milk and juice does he buy altogether?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500354 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c2d3a89a-3b53-50ea-ab1b-27e8bcd50832" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500354 #edb/ref 1074 "We are told that he buys $16$ liters of milk. The tape diagram for liters of milk shows $4$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $16÷4=4$ liters.\n\nNow, we fill the number $4$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/c8/c896618aebed4174005a7d47059eb74e24bc762645b8a46303a07e643c293407.png)\n\nSince there are $6$ boxes corresponding to the liters of juice and milk in total, and each box represents $4$ liters, the total number of liters is:\n\n$$\n4\\times 6=24\n$$\n\nSo, he buys $24$ liters of milk and juice altogether." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500356 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500356 #edb/ref 1069 "q-349287" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500356 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500356 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fa/fac768ca9a6b8bd086b6dd9e44f6b564845bad8cae8a3d1345332f25d5cc3f4c.png)\n\nThe tape diagram above shows the ratio between fiction and nonfiction books in a classroom library. What is the ratio of fiction books to all books?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500356 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c899bac6-ef39-565f-bca3-4cc3481908c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500356 #edb/ref 1074 "The tape diagram for fiction books shows $5$ boxes while the tape diagram has $5+8=13$ boxes in total.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of fiction books to all books is $5:13.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500358 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500358 #edb/ref 1069 "q-349298" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500358 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500358 #edb/ref 1071 "In one minute, Ava can type $3$ words while Ben types $5$ words. Which tape diagram represents the given scenario?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500358 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cc35b4b8-7e0d-5fe0-bbed-0dea389c7b90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500358 #edb/ref 1074 "We are told that:  \n\nIn one minute, Ava can type $3$ words while Ben types $5$ words.\n\nSo, in a tape diagram, Ava's tape must contain $3$ boxes, while the tape corresponding to Ben should have $5$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the diagram is the following:\n\n![](images/31/315542297953311a7ebb8fe1ec63b6f896e0b06a526d49c0accac0837cfb9898.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500370 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500370 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61483" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500370 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500370 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/c0/c00fee9c5165bea605b349ee700e46c2e1898e7c6b65595c462207fd237d6e5a.png)\n\nSally made a necklace using cubic and spherical beads.  The ratio of cubic to spherical beads is given by the tape diagram above.  If there are $18$ spherical beads in the necklace, then how many cubic beads are there in total?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500370 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e4c72bae-b132-52e1-8c37-a59f0f9c3c2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500370 #edb/ref 1074 "We are told that there are $18$ spherical beads in total. The tape diagram for those shows $3$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $18÷3=6$ beads.  \n\nNow, we fill the number $6$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/9b/9b7efbe8e98fe498afbed34ffa33f02248eb72bd3a16a8683a5c26daefda9505.png)\n\nSince there are $5$ boxes corresponding to cubic beads, and each box represents $6$ beads, the number of the cubic beads is:\n\n$$\n5\\times 6=30\n$$\n\nSo, there are $30$ cubic beads in the necklace." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500374 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500374 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61770" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500374 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500374 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7c/7c7e161603d7f4dc59a8d19c4b28326232779c20fc6e029d168ad15e84661aa1.png)\n\nDavid's bag has green and yellow balls, in total there are $40$ balls. The ratio of green balls to yellow balls is shown in the diagram above. How many green balls are there?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500374 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed7cfda9-6dae-5e39-9991-44b62b4e52f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500374 #edb/ref 1074 "The tape diagram shows $3$ boxes corresponding to green, and $5$ boxes corresponding to yellow. Therefore, the ratio of green balls to yellow balls in David's bag is $3:5.$\n\nWe are told that David's bag has $40$ balls in total. The tape diagram has $3+5=8$ boxes in total. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $40÷8=5$ balls in the bag.\n\nNow, we fill the number $5$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/8f/8fdf2dfff7c145ae3774ec869a54752f2fb1c47ad98da3a21b45c36c3e1a9b09.png)\n\nSince there are $3$ boxes corresponding to green balls, and each box represents $5$ balls, the number of green balls must be:\n\n$$\n3\\times 5=15.\n$$\n\nSo, there are $15$ green balls in David's bag." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500379 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500379 #edb/ref 1069 "q-92792" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500379 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500379 #edb/ref 1071 "A survey was conducted among high school students to find out their favorite games. According to their responses, for every $3$ students who prefer soccer, there are $5$ students who prefer baseball. Which tape diagram represents the given scenario?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500379 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7a86a9c-206d-5e61-b545-baa0dd6589ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500379 #edb/ref 1074 "We are told that:  \n\nfor every $3$ students who prefer soccer there are $5$ students who prefer baseball\n\nSo, in a tape diagram, soccer´s tape must contain $3$ boxes, while the tape corresponding to baseball should have $5$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the diagram is the following:\n\n![](images/50/5098abed199db997b901675210c7289f2a85732881a1defeadc2e5f2b80d8086.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
